s4-3-p7 : Block
s4-3-p7 = prose (cons "A quotient identifies specified distinctions; an operation on it must respect those identifications. Other observations may require a different representation. For a type \(X\) and an equivalence relation \(\sim\), a set quotient has point constructors \([x]\), path constructors \([x]=[y]\) for \(x\sim y\), and a set-truncation constructor. For a set-valued codomain \(B\), its elimination rule constructs a function from the quotient to \(B\) from a function \(X\to B\) that respects \(\sim\). Elimination into a higher type requires the corresponding coherence data; a higher inductive presentation can retain nontrivial path structure; higher-inductive semantics have been studied explicitly ([11](#ref-11)). The difference matters for graph symmetries: identifying graphs up to renaming as a set discards the automorphism witnesses that a groupoid-level representation can retain." nil)
